# Implementation plan — Spec 1.17.0

## Summary

Remember the guest’s **requested page** before login. After Identity iframe success (Google or email/password), restore that page instead of always navigating to WebOnOne `/`. Preserve website `return_url` **path + query** (stop stripping to origin root). Invalid targets → default homepage. No open redirects.

See [02-post-login-return-page.md](./02-post-login-return-page.md).

## Branch and prerequisites

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| Branch | `spec/1.17.0` |
| Prerequisite | [1.14.0](../1.14.0/README.md) iframe login + website auth-code handoff |
| Services | WebOnOne FE, Website FE; optional platform-nav |
| New env | None required (`VITE_WEBSITE_ORIGIN`, `VITE_WEBSITE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` already exist) |

---

## Phase 1 — Validate and preserve return targets

**Goal:** Parsers keep deep links; reject unsafe URLs.

**Exit criteria:** Unit tests prove path retention + allowlist rejection.

| Task | Paths |
|------|-------|
| Fix website return parse | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/auth/utils/websiteConfig.ts` |
| Core return path helper | Same auth utils folder (or LoginPage-local) |
| Optional align | `packages/platform-nav/src/returnUrl.ts` |

**Verify:** `npm run type-check -w webonone-v2-root` (+ platform-nav tests if changed)

---

## Phase 2 — Wire login + capture

**Goal:** Post-login restore; CTAs pass current page.

**Exit criteria:** Manual Google + email flows return to deep page.

| Task | Paths |
|------|-------|
| Login host | `LoginPage.tsx`, `IdentityLoginFrame.tsx`, `useIdentityAuthMessage.ts`, `WebsiteReturnRedirect.tsx` |
| Website CTAs | `website/.../webononeConfig.ts` + auth-required call sites |
| Guards | WebOnOne routes that send guests to `/login` |

**Verify:** type-check webonone + website; manual acceptance in [07](./07-implementation-plan.md)

---

## Do not

- Strip website `return_url` to origin root
- Always `navigate('/')` after iframe success when a valid return exists
- Put JWT/password in return URL
- Accept cross-origin returns outside the website allowlist
